1
00:00:02,127 --> 00:00:04,757
(Sheldon:)Your argument is lacking
in all scientific merit.

2
00:00:04,921 --> 00:00:06,501
And it is well-established...

3
00:00:06,673 --> 00:00:10,013
(Sheldon:)...Superman cleans his uniform
by flying into Earth's yellow sun...

4
00:00:10,176 --> 00:00:12,266
(Sheldon:)...which incinerates
any contaminant matter...

5
00:00:12,429 --> 00:00:16,769
(Sheldon:)...and leaves the invulnerable Kryptonian
fabric unharmed and daisy fresh.

6
00:00:18,059 --> 00:00:20,059
(Howard:)What if he gets something
Kryptonian on it?

7
00:00:20,228 --> 00:00:24,148
- Like what?
- I don't know. Kryptonian mustard.

8
00:00:24,315 --> 00:00:27,405
I think we can assume all Kryptonian
condiments were destroyed...

9
00:00:27,569 --> 00:00:30,159
(Sheldon:)...when the planet Krypton exploded.

10
00:00:30,321 --> 00:00:32,281
(Raj:)Or it turned into mustard Kryptonite.

11
00:00:32,449 --> 00:00:36,619
(Raj:)The only way to destroy a rogue
Kryptonian hot dog threatening Earth.

12
00:00:37,537 --> 00:00:40,127
(Leonard:)Raj, please, let's stay serious here.

13
00:00:40,290 --> 00:00:43,830
(Leonard:)Superman's body is Kryptonian,
therefore his sweat is Kryptonian.

14
00:00:44,002 --> 00:00:46,502
(Howard:)Yeah, what about Kryptonian pit stains?

15
00:00:46,963 --> 00:00:48,753
(Sheldon:)Superman doesn't sweat on Earth.

16
00:00:48,923 --> 00:00:51,633
(Howard:)Okay. He's invited for dinner
in the bottle city of Kandor.

17
00:00:51,801 --> 00:00:55,221
(Howard:)He miniaturizes himself, enters the city,
where he loses his super-powers.

18
00:00:55,388 --> 00:00:58,478
(Howard:)Before dinner, his host says,
"Who's up for Kryptonian tetherball?"

19
00:00:58,641 --> 00:01:02,021
Superman works up a sweat, comes back
to Earth, his uniform now stained...

